Z||000000||Raydar||12-10-1999||04:33 PM||||Okay... I'm bummed. Formula has been up on jackstands for last three weeks, with rear brakes disassembled, waiting for me to find the time to put it all back together. Finally got the rear brakes buttoned up, and the car back on the ground. Decided to do the fronts, even though there was still some pad left (warped rotor). Was about 15 minutes from *done* -until I checked that !%$!$&! right front wheel bearing. Suddenly, I'm not gonna be done until tomorrow. (New bearing should be at the store by 8:00 A.M.) Which leads to a technical question... Is the bearing/hub assembly pressed in to the steering knuckle? I've got the three bolts out, but the sucker will_not_budge. If it isn't pressed in, it's rusted in. <BR>Thanks for listening to me vent. I feel better.<BR>(Yes, I know this is a "technical" post, but it didn't start out that way.)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   <p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-10-1999).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||Monkeyman||12-10-1999||08:20 PM||||Don't feel bad about having your car on stands for 3 weeks.  Mine's been sitting all alone in the driveway for over a month now and it will probably be spring before it's roadworthy again.||||reg||1
